### Timeline Extended: the mod's centred popups (Space Race UI pass design § 3,
### docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-31-space-race-ui-pass-design.md). Additive: a
### scripted widget (gui/scripted_widgets/te_systems_window.txt registers the
### root), so no vanilla file is replaced.
###
### te_popups  a full-size root on the popups layer, above the journal panel,
###            the side panels and the Timeline Extended window. It is up only
###            while a popup or the Fleets window is open, for a played country (as the Timeline
###            Extended window's root), and holds one instance of each popup
###            type. Each derives from te_ui_popup (gui/te_widget_library.gui)
###            and shows on its own value of te_popup.
###
### STATE. te_popup is a client-side GetVariableSystem value (never saved): the
### open popup, one at a time. Set by the button that opens a popup, cleared by
### its close button, Escape and a click outside. One window has a key of its
### own beside it, so that a te_popup picker can open over it:
###   sr_fleet_focus     the Fleets window (te_sr_fleet_popup,
###                      space_race_widget.gui; its pages and list generated by
###                      gen_space_fleets.py): a fleet's page, with every fleet
###                      we have listed at its left. Up while the key exists,
###                      its value the slot shown (1 to 9); set by the arrow at
###                      the head of a fleet's card in Space Fleets and by the
###                      window's own list, cleared by its close buttons. The
###                      page's orders open sr_dest_<n>, sr_ftarget_<n>,
###                      sr_xfer_<n> and sr_land_<n> below, which draw over it
###                      (they are instanced after it) and leave it up; while
###                      one is open the window's own close buttons are hidden,
###                      so a click outside closes the picker alone (seen in
###                      game, 2026-11-25), and so should Escape (not yet
###                      tried). Its page may open only popups instanced after
###                      it here: one drawn under it would hide its close
###                      buttons with nothing in reach.
### te_popup's values:
### --- History chart viewers (charts-help-national-info plan, PR C2) ------
###   chart_<id>         a history chart alone at full size, te_chart_<id>_popup:
###                      the round button beside the panel chart's title opens
###                      it. The 33 popups, the range buttons they share with
###                      the panels and te_chart_popups, which holds them, are
###                      generated (gen_te_history_charts.py, into
###                      gui/te_history_charts_generated.gui), each under the
###                      gate and datacontext below; ids are its CHARTS'.
### --- end history chart viewers ------------------------------------------
###   sr_target          Solar System Colonization's colony target
###                      (te_sr_target_popup, space_race_widget.gui)
###   sr_colony          the Colonies window: one colony's page, with every
###                      colony we hold listed at its left (te_sr_colony_popup,
###                      space_race_widget.gui; its pages and list generated
###                      by gen_solar_sites.py). The colony shown is a second
###                      client-side key, sr_colony_focus, set by whatever
###                      opens the window (a colony's name in the Colonies
###                      list, its row in Solar System, its marker on the
###                      system map) and by the window's own list.
###   sr_dest_<n>        fleet slot n's destination (te_sr_dest_popup,
###                      space_race_widget.gui; its bodies are generated by
###                      gen_space_fleets.py, one a slot)
###   sr_ftarget_<n>     fleet slot n's target world (te_sr_ftarget_popup,
###                      likewise)
###   sr_xfer_<n>        a fleet's Transfer (n its slot, 1 to 9; te_sr_xfer_popup,
###                      space_race_widget.gui, its bodies generated by
###                      gen_space_fleets)
###   sr_land_<n>        fleet slot n's Marines: where its marines land and
###                      embark, and how many (te_sr_land_popup, likewise)
### --- Help pages (charts-help-national-info plan, PRs H1 and H2) --------
###   help_<key>         a system's Help page, te_<key>_help_popup (a
###                      te_ui_help_popup), in the system's widget file: its
###                      "How X Works" section, now a link, and the "?" in its
###                      tab's header open it. A page reads GetPlayer only, so
###                      it needs none of the gate and datacontext below.
###                      Pages: banking, grand_monuments, colonial_empire,
###                      cultural_hegemony, nuclear_weapons,
###                      strategic_reserve, seabed, covert_warfare, nation,
###                      budget_breakdown, united_nations, demographics,
###                      tax_code, space_race, global_warming,
###                      power_grids, private_actors,
###                      construction_market (the
###                      construction panel's market section; its types in
###                      gui/construction_panel.gui)
###                      (test_te_help_pages.py's PAGES).
### --- end Help pages ------------------------------------------------------
###
### A popup has no journal entry of its own, so each body sits under the entry's
### scope-free gate and a GetPlayerJournalEntry datacontext on a child, as the
### Timeline Extended window's tabs do (gui_modding_guide.md gotchas #22, #29):
### the rows' JournalEntry.GetCountry reads then work as in the panel.

widget = {
	name = "te_popups"
	size = { 100% 100% }
	layer = popups
	visible = "[And( And( GetMetaPlayer.GetPlayedOrObservedCountry.IsValid, Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver ) ), Or( GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_popup'), GetVariableSystem.Exists('sr_fleet_focus') ) )]"

	### --- History chart viewers (charts-help-national-info plan, PR C2) --
	te_chart_popups = {}
	### --- end history chart viewers --------------------------------------

	te_sr_target_popup = {}
	te_sr_colony_popup = {}
	### The Fleets window, on its own key (sr_fleet_focus): before the four
	### pickers its orders open, so they draw over it.
	te_sr_fleet_popup = {}
	te_sr_dest_popup = {}
	te_sr_ftarget_popup = {}
	te_sr_xfer_popup = {}
	te_sr_land_popup = {}

	### --- Help pages (charts-help-national-info plan, PRs H1 and H2) ----
	te_banking_help_popup = {}
	te_grand_monuments_help_popup = {}
	te_colonial_empire_help_popup = {}
	te_cultural_hegemony_help_popup = {}
	te_nuclear_weapons_help_popup = {}
	te_strategic_reserve_help_popup = {}
	te_seabed_help_popup = {}
	te_covert_warfare_help_popup = {}
	te_nation_help_popup = {}
	te_budget_breakdown_help_popup = {}
	te_united_nations_help_popup = {}
	te_demographics_help_popup = {}
	te_tax_code_help_popup = {}
	te_space_race_help_popup = {}
	te_global_warming_help_popup = {}
	te_power_grids_help_popup = {}
	te_private_actors_help_popup = {}
	te_construction_market_help_popup = {}
	### --- end Help pages ---------------------------------------------------
}
